      "message": "\u003e Patch Set 6:\n\u003e \n\u003e Maciej Żenczykowski, Kernel Networking Developer @ Google\n\u003e \n\u003e Those don\u0027t feel like good reasons.  Indeed the most likely reason for it not being 60 is a bug/mistake/oversight.\n\u003e \n\u003e There\u0027s a reason the sysctl doesn\u0027t even exist in later kernels.\n\nThe initial idea for this is to update the API usage. I would like to provide a safer way to migrate with existing mechanism(i.e. still read from property first). I open b/171360470 to track your suggestion to see if it works for everyone. I will follow up in the bug and submit change if no other objection.",
